{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",

  "$comment": [
    "Corrections applied after reading the V2 MCP docs:",
    "1. Servers nest under mcp.servers. V2 does not place server names directly under mcp.",
    "2. The switch is `disabled`, not `enabled`. An unknown `enabled` field is ignored,",
    "   which would have made OpenCode try to connect on every start even before",
    "   cua-driver was installed.",
    "3. codemode:false keeps these tools on the provider's native tool list. Under the",
    "   default Code Mode they are reached as tools.<server>.<tool>, which makes the",
    "   permission action name ambiguous. Native keeps it predictable.",
    "",
    "Tool naming: OpenCode names an MCP tool <server>_<tool>, replacing characters",
    "other than letters, numbers, _ and - with _. The hyphen survives, so the action",
    "is cua-driver_get_window_state. Verified against the v2.0.22 CLI sanitiser:",
    "  Kr = (e) => e.name.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9_-]/g, \"_\")",
    "The trailing hyphen is a literal member of the set, not a range operator.",
    "Re-derive with scripts/resolve-mcp-permission-action.ps1 after a CLI upgrade."
  ],

  "plugins": ["./.opencode/plugins/computer-use.ts"],

  "mcp": {
    "servers": {
      "cua": {
        "type": "local",
        "command": ["cua-driver", "mcp"],
        "disabled": true,
        "codemode": false,
        "environment": {
          "$comment": [
            "standard allows input to ANY application with no prompt, which is the",
            "driver's own default. Move to bounded once config/cua-bounded.yaml is",
            "reviewed; it requires the manifest AND its approval together.",
            "  CUA_DRIVER_PERMISSION_MODE=bounded",
            "  CUA_DRIVER_CAPABILITY_MANIFEST_FILE=<abs path>/config/cua-bounded.yaml",
            "  CUA_DRIVER_CAPABILITY_MANIFEST_APPROVED=1"
          ],
          "CUA_DRIVER_PERMISSION_MODE": "standard"
        }
      }
    }
  },

  "permissions": [
    { "$comment": "Observation is cheap and repeated; never prompt for it.", "action": "cua-driver_get_*", "resource": "*", "effect": "allow" },
    { "action": "cua-driver_list_*", "resource": "*", "effect": "allow" },
    { "action": "cua-driver_screenshot", "resource": "*", "effect": "allow" },
    { "action": "cua-driver_wait", "resource": "*", "effect": "allow" },
    { "action": "cua-driver_start_session", "resource": "*", "effect": "allow" },

    { "$comment": "Anything that changes the machine asks first.", "action": "cua-driver_click", "resource": "*", "effect": "ask" },
    { "action": "cua-driver_type_text", "resource": "*", "effect": "ask" },
    { "action": "cua-driver_press_key", "resource": "*", "effect": "ask" },
    { "action": "cua-driver_hotkey", "resource": "*", "effect": "ask" },
    { "action": "cua-driver_drag", "resource": "*", "effect": "ask" },
    { "action": "cua-driver_scroll", "resource": "*", "effect": "ask" },
    { "action": "cua-driver_move_cursor", "resource": "*", "effect": "ask" },
    { "action": "cua-driver_launch_app", "resource": "*", "effect": "ask" },
    { "action": "cua-driver_kill_app", "resource": "*", "effect": "ask" },

    { "$comment": "Fallback backend. computer_act covers click, type and key, so ask.", "action": "computer_screenshot", "resource": "*", "effect": "allow" },
    { "action": "computer_screen", "resource": "*", "effect": "allow" },
    { "action": "computer_act", "resource": "*", "effect": "ask" }
  ],

  "media": {
    "image": {
      "max_width": 2000,
      "max_height": 2000,
      "max_base64_bytes": 5242880
    }
  }
}
